  "description": "Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc | 27.5\" mountain bike\nA great introduction to off-road cycling – the Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc combines a durable alloy frame, front suspension and reliable disc brakes for exploring trails and enjoying everyday rides.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc is an entry-level mountain bike designed for riders looking to get started with trail riding and off-road adventures. Featuring an alloy frame with internal cable routing and 27.5\" wheels, it offers a versatile setup for exploring local trails, tackling uneven terrain and enjoying recreational cycling.\nAn 80mm suspension fork with lockout helps absorb bumps and uneven surfaces, providing added comfort and control when riding off-road. The 700mm alloy riser handlebars and Reid MTB grips offer a comfortable, confident steering position, while 2.1\" all-terrain MTB tyres provide reliable grip across trails, gravel paths and mixed surfaces.\nA 3x7-speed drivetrain, featuring Shimano Tourney front and TY300 rear derailleurs, provides a range of gearing options for everyday rides and moderate inclines. Mechanical disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver controlled stopping power in changing conditions, while double-wall alloy rims, a sealed bottom bracket and semi-integrated headset add durability for regular riding.\nWhether you're discovering local trails, exploring gravel paths or looking for a versatile bike for getting outdoors, the Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc offers a dependable starting point for mountain biking.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc is ideal for:\n\nNew mountain bike riders, looking for an entry-level bike to get started with off-road cycling\n\nTrail riding and outdoor adventures, with 80mm front suspension and lockout to help absorb bumps and uneven terrain\n\nEveryday recreational cycling, with a versatile setup for local paths and leisure rides\n\nRiders looking for versatile gearing, with a 3x7-speed drivetrain featuring Shimano derailleurs\n\nReliable stopping power, with mechanical disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nRiding across mixed surfaces, with 27.5\" wheels and 2.1\" all-terrain MTB tyres\n\nRegular recreational use, with a 6061 alloy frame, double-wall rims and durable finishing components",
